# AI Academy Mobile — Flutter Conventions (pointer)

Before changing Dart code, read the canonical sections — this rule does not restate them:

| Need | Read |
|---|---|
| Layering `presentation → domain ← data`, controller shape, navigation, repository pattern, test kinds and widget-test harness | `docs/ai/ARCHITECTURE.md` §1–§4, §7 |
| Endpoints, failure types, auth/session, rules for touching the data layer | `docs/ai/DATA_AND_API.md` (§8 before any API change) |
| Code conventions (doc comments carry reasoning, no `TODO`/`FIXME`, strings, icons, Dart specifics) | `docs/ai/DEVELOPMENT_RULES.md` §6 |
| Screen skeleton, scroll/overflow, screen-test traps | `docs/design-system/SCREEN_PATTERNS.md` |
| Reuse order, state trio, accessibility conventions | `docs/design-system/COMPONENT_PATTERNS.md` §1, §6, §9 |

Every behavioural change needs a test (controller vs `fake_*` repo, repository vs `MockClient`, widget with an injected fake).
